{#
    A definition list as the pairs it is.

    Markdown has no list of definitions. A bullet each — the term in bold,
    what it means under it — is the shape every reader of one agrees on. The
    classifier stays on the term's line behind the colon its own punctuation
    already put there.
#}
{%- autoescape false -%}
{%- for item in node.children -%}
{%- set term -%}**{{ renderNode(item.term)|md_line }}**{% for classifier in item.classifiers %} : {{ renderNode(classifier)|md_line }}{% endfor %}{%- endset -%}
{%- set body -%}{% for definition in item.children %}{{ renderNode(definition)|md_tidy }}

{% endfor %}{%- endset -%}
{{ (term ~ "\n\n" ~ body)|md_indent('- ', '  ') }}
{% endfor %}
{% endautoescape %}